---
import BaseHead from '../components/BaseHead.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
import Header from '../components/Header.astro';
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
	<head>
		<BaseHead
			title="About — Jorge Benavides Aspiazu"
			description="Electrical engineer working across IoT, embedded systems, and AI agent infrastructure."
		/>
		<style>
			main {
				width: 720px;
				max-width: calc(100% - 2em);
				margin: auto;
				padding: 3em 1em;
			}
		</style>
	</head>
	<body>
		<Header />
		<main>
			<h1>About</h1>

			<p>
				I'm Jorge Benavides Aspiazu (jobenas), an electrical engineer focused on
				IoT, connected systems, and the intelligence layer above them.
			</p>

			<p>
				My work spans the full stack: embedded firmware for constrained hardware,
				multi-network deployments across LoRaWAN, LTE-M, and satellite, data
				ingestion pipelines, cloud backends, and AI agent infrastructure that reads
				and reasons across what those pipelines produce.
			</p>

			<p>
				The interesting problems sit at boundaries — between devices and networks,
				between networks and cloud systems, between structured sensor data and
				questions that data can't directly answer. That last boundary is where I've
				been spending more time.
			</p>

			<p>
				I also ship tools. <a href="https://pypi.org/project/phantom-browse/" target="_blank">phantom-browse</a>
				is a stealth browser automation library I published on PyPI — built for
				human-like interaction patterns and session reuse across extended runs.
			</p>

			<p>
				This site is where I write about patterns that hold up in production,
				particularly the ones that only surface once systems grow.
			</p>

			<p>
				Contact: <a href="mailto:me@jobenas.com">me@jobenas.com</a>
			</p>
		</main>
		<Footer />
	</body>
</html>
